  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.2: Package-only fix. The 1.0.1 nuspec declared CoreSystem.Observability.Abstractions 1.0.0 because the package was tagged before the central pin was refreshed. This release declares 1.0.1. No code or API changes.\n      1.0.3: Dependency refresh plus a configuration-binding fix. Dependencies: OpenTelemetry stack 1.19.0 to 1.20.0 (Sdk, Api, Exporter.OpenTelemetryProtocol, Extensions.Hosting and the AspNetCore/Http/Runtime/SqlClient instrumentations); Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 7.1.0 to 7.1.1; System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs pinned to 8.0.2 to clear a Moderate advisory; CoreSystem.Observability.Abstractions refreshed to 1.0.2 (Microsoft.Extensions.Diagnostics.HealthChecks 8.0.32). Fix: each exporter now binds only its own configuration subsection (OpenTelemetry:Tracing, OpenTelemetry:Metrics, OpenTelemetry:Logging) instead of the whole OpenTelemetry section, and an invalid value no longer aborts startup. Previously a malformed value such as a non-numeric Tracing:SamplingProbability threw InvalidOperationException from AddObservability and prevented the host from starting. Invalid values are now reported through Trace and the affected exporter falls back to its defaults; a valid Enabled flag is still honoured so one bad value cannot silently disable tracing or metrics. No public API changes.\n      1.1.0: Targets net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0. No public API or code change; the net9.0 and net10.0 assets are new. Dependency refresh on every TFM: OpenTelemetry, OpenTelemetry.Api, OpenTelemetry.Exporter.OpenTelemetryProtocol and OpenTelemetry.Extensions.Hosting 1.20.0 to 1.20.1 (the OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.* packages stay at 1.20.0 because no 1.20.1 is published for them); CoreSystem.Observability.Abstractions 1.0.2 to 1.1.0. The net9.0 and net10.0 assets also bind the Microsoft.Extensions.* and Serilog.AspNetCore lines matching their TFM.",
